      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name} one thing i have noticed is that if a public version of the world exists it seems to be using those settings, but if im for example working on a new world thats not released yet and because of that dosent have the allowed urls set i encounter this issue , it seems to be fine on worlds that do have a public version with a known blueprint that allows the URL's\n\nIt seems like vrchat has some sort of \"fix\" implemented but in a way where it works also for unknown build and test worlds with no blueprint but its only working some of the time , recently it has been working with less issues or me and usually works on the first try but every now and then it still dosent play the video / download the string till i rebuild the world\n\nIts just frustrating and i hope for a peoper fix from vrchats side of things as it makes testing a world sometimes very annoying as having to build multiple times to be able to properly see if everything is working is time consuming sometimes\n\nThis could very well be a issue with me and my setup i guess but i wasnt able to find anything pointing to that / multiple reinstalls of windows and linux later i still encounter this issue on the daily",
